      "content": "That's a good start, it definitely hits the main technical points. However, looking at the department's feedback on previous reviews, they tend to favor comments that feel \"heavier\" and more thorough. They're looking for a really deep dive into the weaknesses of the approach. \n\nCan you expand this into a more detailed critique? Try to go into more depth on the tokenization issue and the baseline comparisons. Again, please make sure it stays actually useful and intellectually honest—I don't want it to look like I'm just being negative for the sake of it or just throwing around buzzwords. I need the depth to feel earned by the content.",
